{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791640466,"nonce":"AGJVFm/5mfh5FXlTokw2kYCLQhA=","title":"cn pagination rebuilds its whole row on every page change","message":"The row was a Stateful with deps on the page, rebuilding every button, arrow and ellipsis when the page changed, with the active and disabled looks decided at build.\n\nFix: the row is a for_each over slots (first, previous, start ellipsis, the visible page numbers, end ellipsis, next, last) computed from the page, keyed by slot, so a page still in view keeps its button. `cn-pagination-btn--active` and `--disabled` are class_when over the page, and the existing CSS rules paint them; the number's and arrows' colours are computeds; clicks read the page when they happen. PageValue gains `read(\u0026ReactiveGraph)` so a computed follows any of its three representations.\n\nTests: `blinc_cn/tests/pagination_in_place.rs` (active mark moves and a page in view keeps its button; arrows disable at the ends; the page window follows the page), each step checked for subtree rebuilds; all three fail against the old component.","files":null}]}